1
00:00:00,078 --> 00:00:07,120
在接下来的 17 分钟里，我将带大家概览最重要的机器学习算法，
帮助你判断哪种算法适合你的问题。
In the next 17 minutes, I will give you an overview of the most important machine
learning algorithms to help you decide which one is right for your problem.

2
00:00:07,374 --> 00:00:15,200
我叫蒂姆，是一名拥有 10 多年经验的数据科学家，
并在实战机器学习训练营中教给数百名学生这些算法。
My name is Tim, and I have been a data scientist for over 10 years and taught all of
these algorithms to hundreds of students in real-life machine learning boot camps.

3
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:18,240
选择适合你问题的算法有一个简单的策略。
There is a simple strategy for picking the right algorithm for your problem.

4
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:24,800
在 17 分钟内，你将学会如何为任何问题选择正确的算法，
并对每种算法及其相互关系建立基本的直观理解。
In 17 minutes, you will know how to pick the right one for any problem and
get a basic intuition of each algorithm and how they relate to each other.

5
00:00:25,006 --> 00:00:31,588
我的目标是让尽可能多的朋友能够直观地理解主要的机器学习算法，让你不再感到不知所措。
My goal is to give as many of you as possible an intuitive understanding of
the major machine learning algorithms to make you stop feeling overwhelmed.

6
00:00:31,760 --> 00:00:40,200
根据 Wikipedia 的定义，机器学习是人工智能的一个研究领域，
专注于开发和研究能够从数据中学习、并推广到未见数据，
According to Wikipedia, machine learning is a field of study in artificial intelligence concerned with the development and study of
statistical algorithms that can learn from data and generalize to unseen data and thus perform tasks without explicit instructions.

7
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:43,840
从而在没有明确指令的情况下执行任务的统计算法。
According to Wikipedia, machine learning is a field of study in artificial intelligence concerned with the development and study of
statistical algorithms that can learn from data and generalize to unseen data and thus perform tasks without explicit instructions.

8
00:00:44,110 --> 00:00:50,532
近期 AI 的许多进展都由神经网络推动，我希望通过这段视频让你对神经网络有直观的理解。
Much of the recent advancements in AI are driven by neural networks, which
I hope to give you an intuitive understanding of by the end of this video.

9
00:00:50,990 --> 00:00:53,348
让我们把机器学习划分为不同的子领域。
Let's divide machine learning into its subfields.

10
00:00:53,838 --> 00:00:58,720
通常，机器学习分为两个领域：监督学习和无监督学习。
Generally, machine learning is divided into two areas, supervised learning and unsupervised learning.

11
00:00:58,990 --> 00:01:09,924
监督学习是指我们拥有一个包含任意数量自变量（也称为特征或输入变量）以及一个待预测的因
变量（也称为目标或输出变量）的数据集。
Supervised learning is when we have a dataset with any number of independent variables, also called features or input variables,
and a dependent variable, also called target or output variable, that is supposed to be predicted.

12
00:01:10,446 --> 00:01:20,100
我们有一个所谓的训练数据集，其中已知输出变量的真实值（也称为标签），
我们可以用它来训练算法，以便随后预测新未知数据的输出变量。
We have a so-called training data set where we know the true values for the output variable, also called labels,
that we can train our algorithm on to later predict the output variable for new unknown data.

13
00:01:20,366 --> 00:01:31,364
例子可以是预测房屋的价格，即基于房屋特征（如面积、位置、
建造年份等）的输出变量；或者将一个物体分类为猫或狗。
Examples could be predicting the price of a house, the output variable based on features of the house, say square footage, location,
year of construction, etc . categorizing an object as a cat or a dog.

14
00:01:31,854 --> 00:01:37,760
后者是根据对象的特征（如高度、重量、耳朵大小、眼睛颜色等）来确定输出变量或标签。
the output variable or label based on features of the object, say height, weight, size of the ears, color of the eyes, etc.

15
00:01:38,094 --> 00:01:43,440
无监督学习基本上是指任何没有监督的学习问题，也就是说，我们并不了解数据中的真相。
Unsupervised learning is basically any learning problem that is not supervised, so where no truth about the data is known.

16
00:01:43,662 --> 00:01:52,480
因此，监督算法就像是给个小孩看典型的猫和狗长什么样，
然后给他一张新照片并问他看到的是什么动物。
So where a supervised algorithm would be like showing a little kid what a typical cat looks like and what a typical dog looks like,
and then giving it a new picture and asking it what animal it sees.

17
00:01:52,654 --> 00:02:01,360
而无监督算法则是给一个完全不知道猫和狗是什么的孩子的一堆动物图片，
并要求他在没有任何进一步指令的情况下按相似性进行分组。
An unsupervised algorithm would be giving a kid with no idea of what cats and dogs are,
a pile of pictures of animals and asking it to group by similarity without any further instructions.

18
00:02:01,646 --> 00:02:09,124
无监督问题的例子可能是将你的所有邮件分成三个未指定的类别，
然后你再根据自己的意愿去检查并命名它们。
Examples of unsupervised problems might be to sort all of your emails into three unspecified categories,
which you can then later inspect and name as you wish.

19
00:02:09,645 --> 00:02:14,240
算法将自行决定如何创建这些类别，也称为聚类。
The algorithm will decide on its own how it will create those categories, also called clusters.

20
00:02:14,510 --> 00:02:18,884
让我们从监督学习开始，这可以说是机器学习中更大、更重要的分支。
Let's start with supervised learning, arguably the bigger and more important branch of machine learning.

21
00:02:19,214 --> 00:02:20,800
它大致分为两个子类别。
There are broadly two subcategories.

22
00:02:21,040 --> 00:02:25,600
在回归中，我们希望根据给定的输入变量来预测一个连续数值目标变量。
In regression, we want to predict a continuous numeric target variable for a given input variable.

23
00:02:25,838 --> 00:02:33,760
用之前的例子来说，就是根据房屋的若干特征来预测房价，并确定它们与最终房价之间的关系。
Using the example from before, it could be predicting the price of a house given any number of features of a house,
and determining their relationship to the final price of the house.

24
00:02:34,030 --> 00:02:42,308
例如，我们可能会发现面积与价格成正比（线性相关），但房子的房龄对房价没有影响。
We might, for example, find out that square footage is directly proportional to the price, linear dependence,
but that the age of the house has no influence on the price of the house.

25
00:02:42,574 --> 00:02:47,760
在分类中，我们试图给一个数据点分配一个离散类别标签，也称为类别。
In classification, we try to assign a discrete categorical label, also called a class, to a data point.

26
00:02:47,950 --> 00:02:53,060
例如，我们可能想根据邮件的内容、发件人等信息，给一封邮件标注为“垃圾邮件”或“非垃圾邮件”。
For example, we may want to assign the label spam or no spam to an email based on its content, sender, and so on.

27
00:02:53,518 --> 00:02:59,280
但我们也可以有超过两个类别，比如 Gmail 默认提
供的：垃圾邮件、主要、社交和推广，以及更新。
But we could also have more than two classes, for example, junk, primary social promotions, and updates, as Gmail does by default.

28
00:02:59,502 --> 00:03:05,380
现在让我们深入研究具体的算法，从机器学习算法的鼻祖——线性回归开始。
Now let's dive into the actual algorithms, starting with the mother of all machine learning algorithms, linear regression.

29
00:03:05,838 --> 00:03:10,080
通常情况下，监督学习算法试图确定两个变量之间的关系。
In general, supervised learning algorithms try to determine the relationship between two variables.

30
00:03:10,286 --> 00:03:12,560
我们试图找到将一个映射到另一个的函数。
We try to find the function that maps one to the other.

31
00:03:12,910 --> 00:03:20,160
线性回归在最简单的形式下，就是试图确定两个变量（即输入和输出）之间的线性关系。
Linear regression, in its simplest form, is trying to determine a linear
relationship between two variables, namely the input and the output.

32
00:03:20,494 --> 00:03:26,884
我们希望通过最小化数据点与回归线之间距离的平方和，来拟合一个线性方程。
We want to fit a linear equation to the data by minimizing the sum of
squares of the distances between data points and the regression line.

33
00:03:27,246 --> 00:03:35,520
这只是在最小化真实数据与我们的预测模型（在这种情况下是回归线）之间的平均距离，
因此应该能减少新数据点的预测误差。
This simply minimizes the average distance of the real data to our predictive model, in this case the regression line,
and should therefore minimize prediction errors for new data points.

34
00:03:35,694 --> 00:03:45,444
线性关系的一个简单例子是人的身高和鞋码，其中回归拟合可能会告诉我们，
每增加一个单位的鞋码，人的平均身高就会增加两英寸。
A simple example of a linear relationship might be the height and shoe size of a person,
where the regression fit might tell us that for every one unit of shoe size increase, the person will be on average two inches taller.

35
00:03:45,774 --> 00:03:49,520
你可以让模型变得更复杂，并将多维数据拟合到一个输出变量上。
You can make your model more complex and fit multidimensional data to an output variable.

36
00:03:49,742 --> 00:03:55,600
在鞋码的例子中，你可能想要加入性别、年龄和种族等信息，来获得一个更好的模型。
In the example of the shoe size, you might, for example, want to include the gender, age,
and ethnicity of the person to get an even better model.

37
00:03:55,760 --> 00:04:03,920
许多非常高级的机器学习算法，包括神经网络，都只是
这种简单想法的延伸，我稍后会在视频中向你们展示。
Many of the very fancy machine learning algorithms, including neural networks, are
just extensions of this very simple idea, as I will show you later in the video.

38
00:04:04,238 --> 00:04:09,092
逻辑回归是线性回归的一个变体，并且可能是最基础的分类算法。
Logistic regression is a variant of linear regression and probably the most basic classification algorithm.

39
00:04:09,262 --> 00:04:19,360
不再是拟合两个具有假设线性关系的数值变量，而是尝
试使用类别或数值型输入变量来预测一个类别输出变量。
Instead of fitting a line to two numerical variables with a presumably linear relationship,
you now try to predict a categorical output variable using categorical or numerical input variables.

40
00:04:19,598 --> 00:04:20,800
让我们看一个例子。
Let's look at an example.

41
00:04:21,005 --> 00:04:26,240
我们现在想预测两个类别中的一个，例如，根据身高和体重来预测一个人的性别。
We now want to predict one of two classes, for example, the gender of a person based on height and weight.

42
00:04:26,606 --> 00:04:28,868
在这种情况下，线性回归就不太有意义了。
So a linear regression wouldn't make much sense anymore.

43
00:04:29,198 --> 00:04:34,436
我们不再拟合一条线，而是给数据拟合一个所谓的 Sigmoid 函数，它看起来像这样。
Instead of fitting a line to the data, we now fit a so called sigmoid function to the data, which looks like this.

44
00:04:34,958 --> 00:04:44,452
这个方程现在不会告诉我们两个变量之间的线性关系，而是方便地告诉我们，
在给定输入变量的情况下，数据点属于某个类别的概率。
The equation will now not tell us about a linear relationship between two variables,
but will now conveniently tell us the probability of a data point falling into a certain class given the value of the input variable.

45
00:04:44,814 --> 00:04:50,560
例如，一个身高 180 厘米的成年人是男性的可能性为 80%。
So for example, the likelihood of an adult person with a height of 180 centimeters being a man would be 80%.

46
00:04:51,470 --> 00:04:52,912
当然，这只是我随便编的例子。
This is completely made up, of course.

47
00:04:53,358 --> 00:05:00,192
K 最近邻算法，即 KNN，是一种非常简单且直观的算法，可用于回归和分类。
The K nearest neighbors algorithm, or KNN, is a very simple and intuitive
algorithm that can be used for both regression and classification.

48
00:05:00,366 --> 00:05:02,592
它是一种所谓的非参数算法。
It is a so-called non-parametric algorithm.

49
00:05:02,830 --> 00:05:06,884
这个名字意味着我们不试图拟合任何方程，因此也不需要寻找模型的任何参数。
The name means that we don't try to fit any equations and thus find any parameters of a model.

50
00:05:07,118 --> 00:05:08,752
所以不需要进行真正的模型拟合。
So no true model fitting is necessary.

51
00:05:09,006 --> 00:05:14,912
KNN 的核心思想是：对于任何给定的新数据点，我们将目标预测为它最接近的 K 个邻居的平均值。
The idea of KNN is simply that for any given new data point, we will predict the target to be the average of its K nearest neighbors.

52
00:05:15,086 --> 00:05:22,512
虽然这看起来很简单，但它实际上是一个非常强大的预测算法，
尤其是当关系比简单的线性关系更复杂时。
While this might seem very simple, this is actually a very powerful predictive algorithm,
especially when relationships are more complicated than a simple linear relationship.

53
00:05:22,734 --> 00:05:30,432
在分类示例中，我们可以说一个人的性别将与在体重和高度上最接近的五个人的大多数人一致。
In a classification example, we might say that the gender of a person will be the same as
the majority of the five people closest in weight and height to the person in question.

54
00:05:30,766 --> 00:05:37,472
在回归示例中，我们可以说一个人的体重是在身高和胸围上最接近的三个人的平均重量。
In a regression example, we might say that the weight of a person is the
average weight of the three people closest in height and of chest circumference.

55
00:05:37,632 --> 00:05:39,140
这非常符合直觉。
This makes a ton of intuitive sense.

56
00:05:39,342 --> 00:05:42,112
你可能会发现数字三看起来有点随意，而且它确实是随机选的。
You might realize that the number three seems a bit arbitrary, and it is.

57
00:05:42,382 --> 00:05:46,352
K 被称为该算法的一个超参数，选择正确的 k 是一门艺术。
K is called a hyperparameter of the algorithm, and choosing the right k is an art.

58
00:05:46,512 --> 00:05:55,844
选择一个非常小的 K 值，比如一或两个，会导致你的模型对训练数据集预测得很好，
但无法很好地推广到未见数据，这被称为过拟合。
Choosing a very small number of k, say one or two, will lead to your model predicting your training data set very well,
but not generalizing well to unseen data, this is called overfitting.

59
00:05:56,238 --> 00:06:00,964
选择一个很大的数字，比如 1000，会导致整体拟合变差，这被称为欠拟合。
Choosing a very large number, say 1000, will lead to a worse fit overall, this is called underfitting.

60
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:04,512
最佳的数字在两者之间，并且很大程度上取决于当前的问题。
The best number is somewhere in between and depends a lot on the problem at hand.

61
00:06:04,686 --> 00:06:09,712
寻找正确超参数的方法包括交叉验证，但这超出了本视频的范围。
Methods for finding the right hyperparameters include cross-validation but are beyond the scope of this video.

62
00:06:10,062 --> 00:06:17,952
支持向量机是一种监督学习的机器学习算法，最初
是为分类任务设计的，但它也可以用于回归任务。
Support vector machine is a supervised machine learning algorithm originally designed for classification tasks,
but it can also be used for regression tasks.

63
00:06:18,254 --> 00:06:25,072
该算法的核心概念是在数据点之间绘制一条决策边界，尽可能好地将训练集中的数据点分开。
The core concept of the algorithm is to draw a decision boundary between data
points that separates data points of the training set as well as possible.

64
00:06:25,326 --> 00:06:31,392
顾名思义，一个新的未见数据点将根据它相对于决策边界的位置被分类。
As the name suggests, a new unseen data point will be classified according to where it falls with respect to the decision boundary.

65
00:06:31,552 --> 00:06:36,832
让我们拿这个随机的例子：尝试通过动物的重量和鼻子的长度来对它们进行分类。
Let's take this arbitrary example of trying to classify animals by their weight and the length of their nose.

66
00:06:37,070 --> 00:06:41,472
在这个简单的猫和象分类案例中，决策边界是一条直线。
In this simple case of trying to classify cats and elephants, the decision boundary is a straight line.

67
00:06:41,774 --> 00:06:48,752
SVM算法试图找到一条能以最大间隔分隔不同类别的线，也就是说，最大化不同类别之间的空间。
The SVM algorithm tries to find the line that separates the classes with the largest margin possible,
that is maximizing the space between the different classes.

68
00:06:48,974 --> 00:06:53,392
这使得决策边界具有良好的泛化能力，且对训练数据中的噪声和离群值不敏感。
This makes the decision boundary generalize well and less sensitive to noise and outliers in the training data.

69
00:06:53,550 --> 00:06:57,156
所谓的支持向量就是位于间隔边缘的数据点。
The so-called support vectors are the data points that sit on the edge of the margin.

70
00:06:57,454 --> 00:07:02,820
只要知道这些支持向量就足以对新数据点进行分类，这通常使得该算法非常节省内存。
Knowing the support vectors is enough to classify new data points, which often makes the algorithm very memory efficient.

71
00:07:03,214 --> 00:07:06,916
SVM的一个优点是它在高维空间中非常强大。
One of the benefits of SVM is that it is very powerful in high dimensions.

72
00:07:07,310 --> 00:07:10,432
也就是说，当特征数量相对于数据规模很大时。
That is, if the number of features is large compared to the size of the data.

73
00:07:10,638 --> 00:07:13,952
在这些高维情况下，决策边界被称为超平面。
In those higher dimensional cases, the decision boundary is called a hyperplane.

74
00:07:14,112 --> 00:07:21,764
让SVM变得极其强大的另一个特性是使用所谓的核函数，它允许识别高度复杂的非线性决策边界。
Another feature that makes SVMs extremely powerful is the use of so-called kernel functions,
which allow for the identification of highly complex nonlinear decision boundaries.

75
00:07:21,952 --> 00:07:30,272
核函数是一种隐式的方法，利用所谓的核技巧将原始特
征转换为新且更复杂的特征，这超出了本视频的范围。
Kernel functions are an implicit way to turn your original features into new, more complex
features using the so-called kernel trick, which is beyond the scope of this video.

76
00:07:30,542 --> 00:07:38,180
这可以通过创建复杂的新特征（例如体重除以高度的平方，
也称为BMI）来高效地创建非线性决策边界。
This allows for efficient creation of nonlinear decision boundaries by creating complex new features,
such as weight divided by height squared, also called the BMI.

77
00:07:38,318 --> 00:07:39,952
这被称为隐式特征工程。
This is called implicit feature engineering.

78
00:07:40,206 --> 00:07:44,672
神经网络将这种隐式特征工程的概念提升到了更高层次，我稍后会解释。
Neural networks take the idea of implicit feature engineering to the next level, as I will explain later.

79
00:07:44,846 --> 00:07:50,032
SVM可用的核函数包括线性、多项式、RBF和Sigmoid核。
Possible kernel functions for SVMs are the linear, the polynomial, the RBF, and the sigmoid kernel.

80
00:07:50,192 --> 00:07:55,792
另一个相当简单的分类器是朴素贝叶斯分类器，它得名于贝叶斯定理，如下所示。
Another fairly simple classifier is the naive Bayes classifier that gets its name from Bayes' theorem, which looks like this.

81
00:07:56,046 --> 00:08:01,472
我认为通过一个它经常使用的案例——垃圾邮件过滤器，最容易理解朴素贝叶斯。
I believe it's easiest to understand naive Bayes with an example use case that it is often used for, spam filters.

82
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:11,364
我们可以用大量的垃圾邮件和非垃圾邮件来训练算法，统计每个类别中不同词汇出现的次数，
从而计算特定词汇出现在垃圾邮件和非垃圾邮件中的概率。
We can train our algorithm with a number of spam and non-spam emails and count the occurrences of different words in each class,
and thereby calculate the probability of certain words appearing in spam emails and non spam emails.

83
00:08:11,662 --> 00:08:16,420
然后，我们可以利用贝叶斯定理，根据新邮件包含的词语快速对其进行分类。
We can then quickly classify a new email based on the words it contains by using Bayes' theorem.

84
00:08:16,782 --> 00:08:20,196
我们只需将邮件中所有不同词汇的概率相乘即可。
We simply multiply the different probabilities of all words in the email together.

85
00:08:20,622 --> 00:08:27,712
这个算法做出了一个错误的假设，即不同词语出现的概率是相互独立的，
这就是为什么我们称这种分类器为“朴素”的原因。
This algorithm makes the false assumption that the probabilities of the different words
appearing are independent of each other, which is why we call this classifier naive.

86
00:08:28,270 --> 00:08:36,740
这使得它在计算上非常高效，同时仍能很好地近似许多应用场景，
如垃圾邮件分类和其他基于文本的分类任务。
This makes it very computationally efficient while still being a good approximation for
many use cases such as spam classification and other text-based classification tasks.

87
00:08:37,166 --> 00:08:41,058
决策树是许多更复杂的监督学习算法的基础。
Decision trees are the basis of a number of more complex supervised learning algorithms.

