我们可以把它变成一个非常强大的算法。
While this might seem like a very basic and simple algorithm, which it is, we can
turn it into a very powerful algorithm by combining many decision trees together.

96
00:09:18,704 --> 00:09:23,264
将许多简单模型组合成一个更强大、更复杂的模型被称为集成算法。
Combining many simple models to a more powerful, complex model is called an ensemble algorithm.

97
00:09:23,438 --> 00:09:29,668
集成的一种形式是装袋法，即利用一种称为自助采样的方法，
在训练数据的不同子集上训练多个模型。
One form of ensembling is bagging, where we train multiple models on
different subsets of the training data using a method called bootstrapping.

98
00:09:30,062 --> 00:09:38,784
这个想法的一个著名版本叫做随机森林，其中许多决策树
通过随机森林中不同树的多数票来对你的数据进行分类。
A famous version of this idea is called a random forest, where many decision trees vote on the classification of your data by majority
vote of the different trees in the random forest.

99
00:09:39,086 --> 00:09:43,524
随机森林是功能非常强大的估计器，既可用于分类也可用于回归。
Random forests are very powerful estimators that can be used both for classification and regression.

100
00:09:43,950 --> 00:09:52,704
其中的随机性来自于为森林中的不同决策树随机排除某些特征，
这可以防止过拟合并使其更加稳健，因为它消除了树与树之间的相关性。
The randomness comes from randomly excluding features for different trees in the forest,
which prevents overfitting and makes it much more robust because it removes correlation between the trees.

101
00:09:52,974 --> 00:10:04,144
另一种集成方法被称为提升法，它不像随机森林那样并行运行许多决策树，而是按顺序训练模型，
其中每个模型都专注于修复前一个模型所犯的错误。
Another type of ensemble method is called boosting, where instead of running many decision trees in parallel like for random forests,
we train models in sequence, where each model focuses on fixing the errors made by the previous model.

102
00:10:04,334 --> 00:10:07,744
我们将一系列弱模型按顺序组合，从而变成一个强模型。
We combine a series of weak models in sequence, thus becoming a strong model.

103
00:10:07,904 --> 00:10:15,984
由于每个顺序模型都试图修复前一个模型的错误，提升树通
常能获得比随机森林更高的准确率，但也更容易产生过拟合。
Because each sequential model tries to fix the errors of the previous model, boosted trees often get to higher accuracies than random
forests, but are also more prone to overfitting.

104
00:10:16,110 --> 00:10:19,424
它的顺序特性使得它的训练速度比随机森林慢。
Its sequential nature makes it slower to train than random forests.

105
00:10:19,694 --> 00:10:25,984
提升树的著名例子包括 AdaBoost、Gradient Boosting 和 XGBoost，
它们的细节超出了本视频的范围。
Famous examples of boosted trees are AdaBoost, Gradient Boosting,
and XGBoost, the details of which are beyond the scope of this video.

106
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:29,024
现在让我们来看看 AI 领域的霸主：神经网络。
Now let's get to the reigning king of AI, neural networks.

107
00:10:29,294 --> 00:10:32,144
为了理解神经网络，让我们再次看看逻辑回归。
To understand neural networks, let's look at logistic regression again.

108
00:10:32,398 --> 00:10:35,344
假设我们有一系列特征，并试图预测一个目标类别。
Say we have a number of features and are trying to predict a target class.

109
00:10:35,566 --> 00:10:42,144
这些特征可能是数字图像的像素强度，而目标可能是将该图像分类为 0 到 9 之间的某个数字。
The features might be pixel intensities of a digital image, and the
target might be classifying the image as one of the digits from 0 to 9.

110
00:10:42,224 --> 00:10:51,640
