不同的人写出来长得不一样；即使是同一个人多次书写，每次看起来也会略有不同，
Now for this particular case, you might see why this might be difficult to do with logistic regression,
because say the number one doesn't look the same when different people write it, and even if the same person writes it several times,

111
00:10:51,640 --> 00:10:53,530
对于这个特定案例，你可能会发现用逻辑回归很难做到，因为比如数字 1，
不同的人写出来长得不一样；即使是同一个人多次书写，每次看起来也会略有不同，
it will look slightly different each time and it won't be the exact same pixels illuminated for every instance of the number one.

112
00:10:53,530 --> 00:10:56,784
而且并不是每一次都有完全相同的像素点亮。
it will look slightly different each time and it won't be the exact same pixels illuminated for every instance of the number one.

113
00:10:57,024 --> 00:10:59,424
所有这些数字 1 的实例都有共同点。
All of the instances of the number one have commonalities.

114
00:10:59,504 --> 00:11:09,252
例如，它们都有一条明显的垂直线，并且通常不像其他数字那样有交叉线；
而且在数字 1 中通常没有像数字 8 或 9 那样的圆形形状。
However, like they all have a dominating vertical line and usually no crossing lines as other digits might have,
and usually there are no circular shapes in the number one as there would be in the number eight or nine.

115
00:11:09,646 --> 00:11:14,544
然而，计算机最初并不知道这些更复杂的特征，它只知道像素强度。
However, the computer doesn't initially know about these more complex features, but only the pixel intensities.

116
00:11:14,798 --> 00:11:20,464
我们可以通过测量其中一些内容并显式地将它们作为新特征添加进来，来手动构建这些特征。
We could manually engineer these features by measuring some of these things and explicitly adding them as new features.

117
00:11:20,718 --> 00:11:29,904
但人工神经网络，类似于在支持向量机中使用核函数一样，
旨在自动且隐式地为我们设计这些特征，无需人类的引导。
But artificial neural networks, similarly to using a kernel function with a support vector machine,
are designed to implicitly and automatically design these features for us, without any guidance from humans.

118
00:11:30,126 --> 00:11:34,464
我们通过在输入变量和输出变量之间添加额外的未知变量层来实现这一点。
We do this by adding additional layers of unknown variables between the input and output variables.

119
00:11:34,638 --> 00:11:40,224
在最简单的形式下，这被称为单层感知机，它基本上就是一个多特征回归任务。
In its simplest form, this is called a single layer perceptron, which is basically just a multi-feature regression task.

120
00:11:40,462 --> 00:11:45,092
现在如果我们增加一个隐藏层，中间层的隐藏变量就代表了一些隐藏的未知特征。
Now if we add a hidden layer, the hidden variables in the middle layer represent some hidden unknown features.

121
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:53,904
而且我们不再直接预测目标变量，而是尝试用我们的输入特征来预测这些隐藏特征，
然后再尝试用这些新的隐藏特征来预测目标变量。
And instead of predicting the target variable directly, we try to predict these hidden features with our input features,
and then try to predict the target variables with our new hidden features.

122
00:11:54,158 --> 00:12:03,780
在我们的特定例子中，我们可以说每当有几个相邻的像素点亮时，它们就代表一条水平线，
这可以作为一个新特征来尝试预测所涉及的数字，尽管我们从未明确定义过名为“水平线”的特征。
In our specific example, we might be able to say that every time several pixels are illuminated next to each other,
they represent a horizontal line, which can be a new feature to try and predict the digit in question,

123
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:07,172
在我们的特定例子中，我们可以说每当有几个相邻的像素点亮时，它们就代表一条水平线，
