124
00:12:07,598 --> 00:12:12,228
这是对实际情况的一个非常简化的视角，但希望这能说明核心要点。
This is a much simplified view of what is actually going on, but hopefully this gets the point across.

125
00:12:12,622 --> 00:12:14,864
我们通常不知道这些隐藏特征代表什么。
We don't usually know what the hidden features represent.

126
00:12:15,118 --> 00:12:18,624
我们只需训练神经网络尽可能好地预测最终目标。
We just train the neural network to predict the final target as well as possible.

127
00:12:18,894 --> 00:12:22,784
在单隐藏层的情况下，我们能设计的隐藏特征是有限的。
The hidden features we can design this way are limited in the case of the single hidden layer.

128
00:12:22,894 --> 00:12:25,984
但如果我们增加一层，让隐藏层去预测另一个隐藏层呢？
But what if we add a layer and have the hidden layer predict another hidden layer?

129
00:12:26,094 --> 00:12:27,744
如果我们现在有更多层呢？
What if we now had even more layers?

130
00:12:28,014 --> 00:12:37,024
这被称为深度学习，它可以产生非常复杂的隐藏特征，因此
它可能代表图片中各种复杂的信息，比如图中有一个人脸。
This is called deep learning and can result in very complex hidden features, so that might represent all kinds of complex information
in the pictures, like the fact that there is a face in the picture.

131
00:12:37,486 --> 00:12:40,068
然而，我们通常不知道这些隐藏特征的具体含义。
However, we will usually not know what the hidden features mean.

132
00:12:40,302 --> 00:12:42,180
我们只知道它们能产生良好的预测结果。
We just know that they result in good predictions.

133
00:12:42,798 --> 00:12:49,408
到目前为止，我们讨论的都是监督学习，即我们希望利用一些输入变量来预测特定的目标变量。
All we have talked about so far is supervised learning, where we wanted
to predict a specific target variable using some input variables.

134
00:12:49,806 --> 00:12:54,916
然而，有时我们没有什么特定的东西要预测，只是想找出数据中的某些潜在结构。
However, sometimes we don't have anything specific to predict and just want to find some underlying structure in our data.

135
00:12:55,278 --> 00:12:57,060
这就是无监督学习派上用武之处。
That's where unsupervised learning comes in.

136
00:12:57,390 --> 00:12:59,780
一个非常常见的无监督问题是聚类。
A very common unsupervised problem is clustering.

137
00:13:00,046 --> 00:13:04,260
很容易把聚类和分类混淆，但它们在概念上非常不同。
It's easy to confuse clustering with classification, but they are conceptually very different.

138
00:13:04,558 --> 00:13:11,968
分类是指我们知道想要预测的类别，并且拥有带有真实标
签的训练数据，在这里显示为颜色，比如猫和狗的图片。
Classification is when we know the classes we want to predict and have training data
with true labels available, shown as colors here, like pictures of cats and dogs.

139
00:13:12,302 --> 00:13:20,288
聚类则是指我们没有任何标签，只是通过观察数据的整体结构来寻找未知的簇，
并试图在数据中找出潜在的聚类。
Clustering is when we don't have any labels and want to find unknown clusters just by looking at the overall structure of the data and
trying to find potential clusters in the data.

140
00:13:20,494 --> 00:13:23,556
例如，我们可能会看一个像这样的二维数据集。
For example, we might look at a two-dimensional data set that looks like this.

141
00:13:23,854 --> 00:13:26,532
任何人都很可能很容易在这里看到三个聚类。
Any human will probably easily see three clusters here.

142
00:13:26,990 --> 00:13:30,368
但并不总是这么简单，因为你的数据也可能看起来像这样。
But it's not always as straightforward as your data might also look like this.

143
00:13:30,862 --> 00:13:33,924
我们不知道有多少个聚类，因为这是一个无监督问题。
We don't know how many clusters there are because the problem is unsupervised.

144
00:13:34,350 --> 00:13:37,476
最著名的聚类算法被称为K-means聚类。
The most famous clustering algorithm is called k-means clustering.

145
00:13:37,934 --> 00:13:42,724
就像KNN一样，K是一个超参数，代表你正在寻找的聚类数量。
Just like for KNN, K is a hyperparameter and stands for the number of clusters you are looking for.

146
00:13:43,246 --> 00:13:50,116
找到正确的聚类数量同样是一门艺术，这与你的具体问题密切相关，
并且可能需要一些基于领域知识的尝试和错误。
Finding the right number of clusters again is an art and has a lot to do with your specific problem,
and some trial and error in domain knowledge might be required.

147
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:52,100
这超出了本视频的范围。
This is beyond the scope of this video.

148
00:13:52,526 --> 00:13:53,764
K-Means非常简单。
K-Means is very simple.

149
00:13:54,158 --> 00:14:00,196
你首先随机选择K个聚类的中心，并将所有数据点分配到离它们最近的聚类中心。
You start by randomly selecting centers for your K clusters and assigning all data points to the cluster center closest to them.

150
00:14:00,622 --> 00:14:02,528
这里的聚类分别显示为蓝色和绿色。
The clusters here are shown in blue and green.

151
00:14:02,798 --> 00:14:06,500
然后你根据当前分配给它们的点重新计算聚类中心。
You then recalculate the cluster centers based on the data points now assigned to them.

152
00:14:06,926 --> 00:14:09,540
你可以看到中心正向实际的聚类移动。
You can see the centers moving closer to the actual clusters.

153
00:14:09,966 --> 00:14:14,788
接着你再次将数据点分配到新的聚类中心，然后再次重新计算聚类中心。
You then assign the data points again to the new cluster centers, followed by recalculating the cluster centers.

154
00:14:15,566 --> 00:14:19,168
你重复这个过程，直到聚类中心稳定下来。
You repeat this process until the centers of the clusters have stabilized.

155
00:14:19,534 --> 00:14:28,960
虽然K-means是最著名且最常用的聚类算法，但还有其他算法，
包括一些不需要指定聚类数量的算法，比如层次聚类和DBSCAN，
While k-means is the most famous and most common clustering algorithm, other algorithms exist,
including some where you don't need to specify the number of clusters, like hierarchical clustering and db scan,

156
00:14:28,960 --> 00:14:29,770
它们可以找到任意形状的聚类，但我不会在这里讨论它们。
While k-means is the most famous and most common clustering algorithm, other algorithms exist,
including some where you don't need to specify the number of clusters, like hierarchical clustering and db scan,

157
00:14:29,770 --> 00:14:33,380
它们可以找到任意形状的聚类，但我不会在这里讨论它们。
which can find clusters of arbitrary shape, but I won't discuss them here.

158
00:14:33,646 --> 00:14:37,008
我最后留给你们的算法类型是降维。
The last type of algorithm I will leave you with is dimensionality reduction.

159
00:14:37,262 --> 00:14:43,488
降维的思路是减少数据集中的特征或维度，同时尽可能保留信息。
The idea of dimensionality reduction is to reduce the number of features
or dimensions of your data set, keeping as much information as possible.

160
00:14:43,854 --> 00:14:51,968
通常这类算法通过寻找现有特征之间的相关性，并移除可能冗余的维度，
从而在不损失太多信息的情况下完成这一过程。
Usually this group of algorithms does this by finding correlations between existing
features and removing potentially redundant dimensions without losing much information.

161
00:14:52,334 --> 00:14:58,928
例如，要识别出照片里的飞机，你真的需要一张高分辨率的照片吗？
还是说你可以减少图像中的像素数量？
For example, do you really need a picture in high resolution to recognize the airplane in the picture,
or can you reduce the number of pixels in the image?

162
00:14:59,150 --> 00:15:09,980
因此，降维能让你了解现有特征之间的关系，它也可以作为监督学习算法的预处理步骤，
来减少数据集中的特征数量，从而让算法更高效、更稳健。
As such, dimensionality reduction will give you information about the relationships within your existing features,
and it can also be used as a pre-processing step in your supervised learning algorithm to reduce the number of features in your

163
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:12,580
因此，降维能让你了解现有特征之间的关系，它也可以作为监督学习算法的预处理步骤，
来减少数据集中的特征数量，从而让算法更高效、更稳健。
dataset and make the algorithm more efficient and robust.

164
00:15:12,974 --> 00:15:17,088
一个典型的算法是主成分分析，也就是 PCA。
An example algorithm is principal component analysis, or PCA.

165
00:15:17,422 --> 00:15:23,172
假设我们正尝试根据长度、高度、颜色和牙齿数量等几个特征来预测鱼的种类。
Let's say we are trying to predict types of fish based on several features like length, height, color, and number of teeth.

166
00:15:23,438 --> 00:15:33,008
在观察不同特征的相关性时，我们可能会发现高度和长度高度相关，
同时包含这两个特征对算法没啥帮助，甚至可能因为引入噪声而产生负面影响。
When looking at the correlations of the different features, we might find that height and length are strongly correlated,
and including both won't help the algorithm much, and might in fact hurt it by introducing noise.

167
00:15:33,230 --> 00:15:36,288
我们可以简单地加入一个形状特征，它是这两个特征的结合体。
We can simply include a shape feature that is a combination of the two.

168
00:15:36,430 --> 00:15:42,500
这在大型数据集中非常常见，它能让我们大幅减少特征数量，同时还能获得不错的结果。
This is actually extremely common in large datasets and allows us to
reduce the number of features dramatically and still get good results.

169
00:15:42,990 --> 00:15:47,076
PCA 的做法是寻找能够保留数据集中大部分方差的方向。
PCA does this by finding the directions in which most variants in the dataset is retained.

170
00:15:47,374 --> 00:15:50,276
在这个例子中，包含大部分方差的方向是一条对角线。
In this example, the direction of most variants is a diagonal.

171
00:15:50,446 --> 00:15:54,928
这被称为第一个主成分，或者叫 PC，它可以成为我们新的形状特征。
This is called the first principal component, or PC, and can become our new shape feature.

172
00:15:55,182 --> 00:16:03,248
第二个主成分与第一个主成分正交，且只能解释数据集中一小部分的方差，
因此在这种情况下可以从数据集中剔除。
The second principal component is orthogonal to the first and only explains a small fraction of the variants of the dataset and can
thus be excluded from our dataset in this case.

173
00:16:03,502 --> 00:16:13,248
在大型数据集中，我们可以对所有特征这样做，按它们解释的方差进行排序，
并剔除那些对方差贡献不大、也就不会对我们的机器学习模型有太大帮助的主成分。
In large datasets, we can do this for all features and rank them by explain variants and exclude any principal components that don't
contribute much to the variants and thus wouldn't help much in our ML model.

174
00:16:13,422 --> 00:16:15,968
以上就是所有常用机器学习算法的讲解。
This was all common machine learning algorithms explained.

